Local patch (not upstream).

PR #1380 adds `strikethrough`, which makes `attribute_type` exactly fill the
8-bit `attributes` bitfield (SIZE == 8). A ninth attribute would be silently
truncated, and the symptom would be a rendition that simply never renders --
not a build error. This turns that into a compile-time failure.

Suggested by a reviewer on the upstream PR:
https://github.com/mobile-shell/mosh/pull/1380

--- a/src/terminal/terminalframebuffer.h
+++ b/src/terminal/terminalframebuffer.h
@@ -70,6 +70,11 @@
   uint64_t background_color : 25;
   uint64_t attributes : 8;
 
+  /* `attributes` is exactly full at SIZE == 8. Widening it to :14 would still
+     fit, since 25 + 25 + 14 == 64 bits. */
+  static_assert( static_cast<int>( SIZE ) <= 8,
+                 "attribute_type outgrew Renditions::attributes; widen the bitfield" );
+
 public:
   Renditions( color_type s_background );
   void set_foreground_color( int num );
